From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ARM: configs: gts28ltexx_cpufreq: the daily kernel with
 A53 scaling

The daily build of the stage 1 tables: the modem fragment's lines first,
unchanged, then cpufreq-dt as a module that udev loads from the root,
after the initramfs's watchdog guard, schedutil by default, the
userspace and performance governors for cpufreq.sh, CPU cooling, and
the soft lockup and hung task detectors of the soak.

The dtsi and the board say so: the test kernels still blacklist
cpufreq-dt and load it by hand, the daily kernel does not.

Passed on the tablet on 2026-11-03: a 2 hour soak from RECOVERY with the
CP online and the persistent root, then BOOT and four clean reboots.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi        | 10 +++--
 .../dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts     |  2 +-
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config    | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi
index 847b9532b..4379d9baa 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi
@@ -4,10 +4,12 @@
  * scaling, stage 1 for the A53s (docs/hardware/CPUFREQ.md in the
  * omarchy-tab-s2 repository).
  *
- * TEST KERNELS ONLY, with gts28ltexx_cpufreq_test.config: cpufreq-dt is a
- * module, blacklisted at boot (t715.modblacklist=cpufreq_dt) and loaded by
- * hand, so a bad table cannot hang the boot before the initramfs guard
- * (CPUFREQ.md section 8.3).
+ * Two builds use it. The test kernels (gts28ltexx_cpufreq_test.config) blacklist
+ * the cpufreq-dt module at boot (t715.modblacklist=cpufreq_dt) and load it by
+ * hand (CPUFREQ.md section 8.3). The daily kernel since 2026-11-03
+ * (gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config, after stage 1 and the 2-hour soak) lets udev
+ * load it from the root. In both, cpufreq-dt stays a module, so a bad table
+ * cannot hang the boot before the initramfs guard.
  *
  * The voltages are this chip's, not the SoC's: ASV table version 8, group 1,
  * as the stock kernel logged them at every boot of this tablet (CPUFREQ.md
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/samsung/exynos5433-gts28ltexx.dts
